{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>With this shall Aaron come into the sanctuary: with a bull of the herd, etc.</b> And they said in the Midrash (Leviticus Rabbah 21:11): the bull corresponds to Abraham, as it says (Genesis 18:7) ״וְאֶל הַבָּקָר רָץ אַבְרָהָם״; and the ram corresponds to Isaac, whose substitute was offered as a ram; and the two goats correspond to Jacob, as it is said of him (ibid. 27:9) ״וְקַח לִי מִשָּׁם שְׁנֵי גְּדָיֵי עִזִּים״. The intent of this Midrash is to say that just as we find that even to Moses HaShem did not appear except in the merit of the fathers, as it is written (Exodus 4:5): ״לְמַעַן יַאֲמִינוּ כִּי נִרְאָה אֵלֶיךָ ה׳ אֱלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתָם אֱלֹהֵי אַבְרָהָם״ etc., so too the High Priest on Yom Kippur — HaShem appears to him in the merit of the fathers. And there is in all of them an allusion to Yom Kippur, for regarding what is written ״וְאֶל הַבָּקָר רָץ אַבְרָהָם״, this Midrash maintains that it was on Yom Kippur — for our Rabbis of blessed memory also darshaned (in Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 29) ״בְּעֶצֶם הַיּוֹם נִמּוֹל אַבְרָהָם״ that Abraham was circumcised on Yom Kippur, and it maintains that the entire episode from וַיֵּרָא ה׳ אֶל אַבְרָם בְּאֵלוֹנֵי מַמְרֵא all happened on a single day, and even though he made a feast on that day, in any case, since the Torah had not yet been given, he was stringent upon himself and not upon others. And as for the ram of Isaac, there is in the Midrash that that episode was on Yom Kippur (see Yalkut Reubeni, parashat Vayera 22:14), and its proof is from the verse ״אֲשֶׁר יֵאָמֵר הַיּוֹם בְּהַר ה׳ יֵרָאֶה״ — that in every year on this day, HaShem will be seen, for בֶּעָנָן יֵרָאֶה שָׁמָּה ה׳. And the two goats of Jacob — they said in the Midrash (Bereshit Rabbah 65:14) on ״שְׁנֵי גְּדָיֵי עִזִּים טוֹבִים״: good for you and good for your children; good for you, for through them you will receive the blessings; and good for your children, for through them atonement is made for them on Yom Kippur. And from then Jacob was assured of the atonement of this holy day by means of the two goats."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:36:52.701462180Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}